      "class Check { constructor(name) {...} run() {...} } is syntax over JavaScript's prototype inheritance: extends and super(...) mirror Java's OOP (the previous block) almost word for word. Methods live on the class; instances carry the fields set in the constructor via this.",
      "Optional chaining config.options?.timeout returns undefined instead of throwing when a level is missing; paired with ?? it gives safe defaults (?? 5). On untrusted API data this pair replaces the TypeError roulette of deep property access.",
      "Rest (...rest) in destructuring gathers the remainder ([first, ...rest]); spread expands. Map is the key→value structure with any-type keys and guaranteed insertion order (the honest version of abusing objects); Set is uniqueness with fast has — the collections contracts from Java, in JS form.",
