  "l4-shm-bash-control": { task: "[ \"$count\" -gt 5 ] errors with 'integer expression expected' when count holds 'five'. The lesson-grade handling:", options: ["Use = instead", "Validate the shape BEFORE the numeric test (a case/regex digit check), or compare as string deliberately — numeric operators demand numeric text", "Add quotes twice", "Ignore the error"], answer: 1, explain: "Operator families follow types: -gt on non-numeric text is a type error — validate at the layer before, as in every language here.", hint: "Which layer should have caught 'five'?" },
  "l4-shm-bash-loops": { task: "A value-returning function prints a progress line to stdout AND echoes its result. $(func) captures:", options: ["Only the result", "BOTH lines glued together — stdout is one channel; diagnostics belong on stderr (>&2)", "Only the progress", "An error"], answer: 1, explain: "The two-channel rule: stdout carries values, stderr carries diagnostics. Mixing them corrupts captured values silently.", hint: "Where do progress messages belong in a value function?" },
  "l4-shm-bash-text": { task: "A shared log must hide ALL occurrences of IP 203.0.113.44 on every line. The correct sed is:", options: ["sed 's/203.0.113.44/<ip>/' log", "sed 's/203\\.0\\.113\\.44/<ip>/g' log — escaped dots (literal) and /g (every occurrence per line)", "sed 's/203/<ip>/' log", "grep -v 203 log"], answer: 1, explain: "Two traps in one command: unescaped dots match any character, and without /g only the first occurrence per line is masked — a half-masked log is a leak.", hint: "Dots are regex; /g is scope." },
  "l4-shm-bash-files": { task: "An evidence directory must be: owner full access, group read+enter, others nothing. The chmod pair is:", options: ["755 dir, 644 file", "750 on the directory (rwx r-x ---) and 640 on files (rw- r-- ---)", "777 everywhere to avoid errors", "700 dir, 600 file — group gets nothing, failing the requirement"], answer: 1, explain: "Translate each triad: dir 7/5/0, file 6/4/0. 700/600 is tighter than asked — it breaks the group's stated access.", hint: "Directories need x to enter; files need r to read." },
